  "instructions": [
    "Preheat oven to 375°F (190°C).",
    "Cook pappardelle according to package instructions until al dente. ",
    "In a large skillet, sauté chopped onion, minced garlic, and diced bell pepper until softened. ",
    "Add canned diced tomatoes, salt, and pepper to the skillet and stir to combine.",
    "In a large bowl, combine cooked pappardelle, tomato mixture, and melted manteca. ",
    "Stir in coconut milk until well combined.",
    "Transfer the pasta mixture to a 9x13 inch baking dish and top with chopped parsley.",
    "Bake for 25 minutes, or until the top is golden brown and the pasta is heated through.",
    "Remove from the oven and let cool for a few minutes before serving."
  ],
